@startuml
!theme plain
hide footbox
autonumber "<b>(0)</b>"

' --- STILE VISIVO ---
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #2C3E50
    LifeLineBorderColor #2C3E50
    LifeLineBackgroundColor White

    ParticipantBorderColor #2C3E50
    ParticipantBackgroundColor White
    ParticipantFontName Helvetica
    ParticipantFontSize 14
    ParticipantFontStyle bold

    BoxFontSize 16
    BoxFontColor White
}

' --- ATTORI ---

box "Simulation Layer (The World Engine)" #4A90E2
    participant "World State" as World
    participant "Spatial Translator" as Sense
    participant "Rules Oracle" as Oracle
end box

box "Cognitive Layer (The Brain)" #27AE60
    participant "Nation Agent\n(Cabinet)" as Agent
end box

box "Data Layer" #95A5A6
    database "Log Repository" as DB
end box

' --- INIZIO FLUSSO ---

== Phase 1: Sense (Perception) ==

World -> Sense : Send Raw Topology & Resources

activate Sense
Sense -> Sense : Abstract Spatial Features
Sense -> Agent : <b>Inject Strategic Context</b>
note right: Report in linguaggio naturale\n(Minacce, Opportunità, Bilancio)
deactivate Sense

== Phase 2: Think (Reasoning) ==

activate Agent
Agent -> Agent : <b>Cabinet Deliberation</b>
note right of Agent
  Il sistema multi-agente elabora:
  1. Analisi dei Ministri e sentiment popolare
  2. Sintesi del Presidente
  3. Allocazione Budget
end note

Agent -> Oracle : <b>Submit Diplomatic Envelope</b>
note right
  Contiene il <b>Multi-Payload</b>:
  - Azione Militare
  - Azione Economica
  - Azione Estera
end note
deactivate Agent

== Phase 3: Act (Validation & Execution) ==

activate Oracle
Oracle -> Oracle : <b>Validate Constraints</b>
note left
  Verifica sequenziale:
  2. Check Costi vs Budget
  3. Check Fattibilità Fisica
end note

Oracle -> World : <b>Execute State Changes</b>
note left: Aggiorna confini, risorse e\nTrust Matrix nel motore fisico

== Phase 4: Trace (Logging) ==

Oracle -> DB : <b>Archive Turn Data</b>
note right: Salva lo snapshot completo\nper l'Explainability e Replay

World -> World : Advance Turn
deactivate Oracle

@enduml